From 566178daecfbbffbb455244596bc20bf0005210a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Juan Manuel Lopez Carrillo <juanmanuellopezcarrillo@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 02:43:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 057/130] config: disable RESET_GPIO - breaks
 mmc-pwrseq-simple with #gpio-cells=3 (WiFi AP6256 on mmc1)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The reset-GPIO fallback of the reset core only supports #gpio-cells=2
(__reset_add_reset_gpio_device returns -ENOENT with the 3 cells of sunxi),
and with RESET_GPIO enabled IS_ENABLED activates that path in pwrseq_simple
-> probe -2 -> mmc1 never probes. Without RESET_GPIO, pwrseq uses the classic
devm_gpiod_get_array path (equivalent to the BSP 5.15).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .config | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/.config b/.config
index 28091ecf1..7bd92f1a7 100644
--- a/.config
+++ b/.config
@@ -8078,7 +8078,7 @@ CONFIG_PARTITION_PERCPU=y
 # CONFIG_IPACK_BUS is not set
 CONFIG_ARCH_HAS_RESET_CONTROLLER=y
 CONFIG_RESET_CONTROLLER=y
-CONFIG_RESET_GPIO=m
+# CONFIG_RESET_GPIO is not set
 # CONFIG_RESET_MCHP_SPARX5 is not set
 CONFIG_RESET_NUVOTON_MA35D1=y
 CONFIG_RESET_SCMI=y
